  "notes": "GAAP. Governmental lines from governmental funds Statement of Revenues, Expenditures and Changes in Fund Balance (p4, Total Governmental Funds column); business-type from proprietary Statement of Revenues, Expenses, Changes in Net Position (p6, Total column). Business-type receipts total is computed because the statement prints operating revenues and a nonoperating total net of interest expense; interest expense shown as a disbursement. Balance sheet uses government-wide Statement of Net Position Totals column. Governmental fund transfers out 11,026 = business-type transfers in 11,026 (matches). Detail holds the only supplementary schedule (p9, Budget and Actual - All Funds, budgetary basis), fund 'All funds', with budget_final from the Original and Final Budget column (a printed '-' is 0). Its lines mix governmental and utility funds: expenditure functions are tagged by fund type with the function or utility name as department; the Interest and Other revenue lines are split by fund type using p4 and p6 (split_from set; budget_final on the governmental part). Miscellaneous (actual -, budget 997,650) is included as a zero line. Report rounding gaps (p1, p3, p4, p6, p7, p9) are in report_discrepancies. v8 re-trim gained p2 Statement of Activities and p8 cash flow reconciliation; both tie to existing figures. Roll-forward governmental: 614,142 + 621,226 - 1,061,436 - 11,026 = 162,906 (with itemized receipts 621,225 the difference is 1, see report_discrepancies). Read pages 1-9 of 9"
}
